Z||000000||PocketRocket||12-17-2000||04:20 PM||||I noticed mt wheel leaning in at the top one day so I parked the car and left it there, my dad comes home and drives it and the wheel falls off.  It seems the rear lower ball joint had come out.  When it came out it bent the whole assmebly (disc brake and shocks) around and we can't figure out what could be holding it and keeping it from being turned back straight.  We have let it sit in the yard long enough and my grandmom backed into it so now it has a whole in the side to go along with it(just a side note, you can see some damage in the second pic).  Any help would be appreciated, I enclosed some pics.  Thanks in advance.<BR> <A HREF="http://pages.prodigy.net/fourtrax200/Fiero1.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://pages.prodigy.net/fourtrax200/Fiero1.jpg</A>  <P><A HREF="http://pages.prodigy.net/fourtrax200/Fiero2.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://pages.prodigy.net/fourtrax200/Fiero2.jpg</A>  <P><A HREF="http://pages.prodigy.net/fourtrax200/Fiero3.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://pages.prodigy.net/fourtrax200/Fiero3.jpg</A> <P>------------------<BR>-Larry B<BR>'85 SE 2.8L<p>[This message has been edited by PocketRocket (edited 12-17-2000).]||||reg||8
Z||000001||batboy||12-17-2000||08:03 PM||||Looks like at the very least, you need a new strut and rotor. I can't tell if the control arm got bent or if the tie rod is ok. Make sure the wheel bearings are still good too.||||reg||1
